# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/
.cursor/mcp.json

# Build output
/bin/
/dist/

# Satellites colocated state (V5 .satellites/ pattern — see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md).
# Use `.satellites/*` (glob) not `.satellites/` (directory): a directory
# exclude blocks every re-include underneath it; the glob form excludes
# the contents while leaving the directory traversable, so the negation
# rules below actually take effect.
.satellites/*
# Filebased seeds at .satellites/seeds/ are version-controlled (operator-
# authored substrate config; see docs/seeds.md).
!.satellites/seeds/
# File-based documents at .satellites/documents/ are version-controlled
# (operator-authored principles + free-form docs; see docs/document-upload.md).
!.satellites/documents/

# Operator-supplied config — may contain OAuth client secrets. The
# `*.example` templates stay in git; the live files do not.
/scripts/satellites-server.toml
/satellites.toml
